      "extract": "In this section we give a brief exposition of left-invariant total ordering of braid groups called Dehornoy ordering, and define Dehornoy floor. Dehornoy floor is first introduced in [@mn], though they do not use term Dehornoy floor. This is a measure of how far braid is from the identity elements with respect to Dehornoy ordering and can be seen as some kinds of complexity of braids. We describe fundamental results",
